  "_comment": "Employers with graduate schemes or new-grad programmes, shown in the 'PSW & OPT employers' directory. UK rows (country GB) are for Graduate visa (PSW) holders: the Graduate visa lets you work for any employer without sponsorship, and these employers also hold a sponsor licence, so you can switch to a Skilled Worker visa later. US rows are for F-1 OPT / STEM OPT holders: these employers file H-1B petitions (the usual next step after OPT). Every run re-checks each employer against the official register for its country (UK Home Office, USCIS H-1B data) and shows the result; employers discovered in the live feed with entry-level sponsored roles are added automatically, which is where most small and mid-size employers come from. register_name: the legal name on the register when it differs from the brand (a list is allowed). size: large (250+ staff) / medium (50-249) / small (<50). UK rows: every vacancy at the employer is fetched from Adzuna (company search); search: {what_and, aliases} when Adzuna lists the employer under another name, false to skip (the employer has its own careers-site connector); reed: true to also search Reed. careers_url: the employer's own careers site, linked from the directory and from job-board adverts at the employer (board links can be closed outside their country).",
